cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its simulation results, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "Physical-time consistency in learned robot dynamics: AffineFlow"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/physical-time-consistency"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/physical-time-consistency"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
date-released: "2026-10-10"
abstract: >-
  Research software for testing physical-time action-effect structure in learned
  robot dynamics. AffineFlow predicts local acceleration drift and torque response
  and uses known actuator dynamics in a two-evaluation transition map. The completed
  compute-matched simulation study compares it against two mechanics-structured
  neural ODE predictors on one fully observed two-link arm with known actuator lag,
  across 38 training seeds and 4,560 paired control episodes. The supported control
  advantage is modest and conditional on the specified plant, corpus and MPC cost;
  prediction and inference-speed advantages depend on state stratum and batching.
keywords:
  - robot dynamics
  - model predictive control
  - neural ODE
  - physical time
  - actuator dynamics
  - reproducible simulation
